   $q$Why did Ramaswami argue that protecting the petrels directly would not work?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The petrels were too few by then to recover without birds from other islands.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Mainland farms would accept the goats only if the petrels were moved first.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The goats competed with the petrels for the same seeds and shrubs as food.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-relationship"},{"text":"While goats kept the slopes bare, the soil the birds needed could not return.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$While goats kept the slopes bare, the soil the birds needed could not return.$q$, $q$Paragraph 3 says her argument "rested on the link between the animals and the soil," since bare slopes left no ground to burrow in. The passage never says goats and petrels competed for food.$q$, 'draft', '23ab564f-f711-5f7d-9ead-b0371f0f5419')
