   $q$In paragraph 1, the word "arbitrary" most nearly means:$q$, $q$[{"text":"based on chance or whim rather than reason","is_correct":true},{"text":"carefully calculated by experts","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"strictly required by the law","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"extremely old and traditional","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$based on chance or whim rather than reason$q$, $q$The units were chosen by custom or "the size of some long-forgotten official's foot rather than by any consistent principle," so arbitrary means based on whim rather than reason. Old age is part of the description, but it does not capture the key idea of lacking a reason.$q$, 'draft', 'e37da047-2bee-568c-af25-28a37df398a5')
