   $q$Which meaning of "provincial" fits the way the reformers use it in paragraph 2?$q$, $q$[{"text":"located in the countryside, away from cities","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"other-meaning-of-word"},{"text":"dishonest and unfair to buyers","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"modern and shared across the nation","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"narrow and limited to local habits","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$narrow and limited to local habits$q$, $q$The reformers restate the word as "rooted in the narrow habits of individual districts." Provincial can also mean rural, but the complaint here is about narrowness, not location, and cheating was a result of the confusion rather than the meaning of the word.$q$, 'draft', 'e37da047-2bee-568c-af25-28a37df398a5')
