   $q$In paragraph 3, "The need for fair trade provided the impetus for change." What does "impetus" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"an obstacle that slows progress","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"a detailed official plan","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"a driving force or motivation","is_correct":true},{"text":"the final result of an effort","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$a driving force or motivation$q$, $q$Paragraph 2 describes problems that made fair trade necessary, and paragraph 3 shows scientists acting because of that need, so the impetus is the force that pushed change forward. It is the cause of the change, not its final result.$q$, 'draft', 'e37da047-2bee-568c-af25-28a37df398a5')
