   $q$According to the definition in paragraph 3, a "gambit" is:$q$, $q$[{"text":"any opening move in a game of chess","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-broad"},{"text":"a trick that quietly breaks the rules","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"a planned sacrifice made to gain a later advantage","is_correct":true},{"text":"a move that wins a piece at no cost","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$a planned sacrifice made to gain a later advantage$q$, $q$After the colon, the coach's definition says a player "deliberately gives something up, hoping to gain a stronger position." The pawn looked free to Priya, but paragraph 4 shows it had a real cost, so a gambit is not a move that wins at no cost.$q$, 'draft', 'd3f73304-a08e-58b6-95d5-044d1fa76b4a')
