  ('cc272320-d75d-5746-aca8-eb4e8739c96c', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-context-clues'), null, 'hard',
   $q$In paragraph 5, part of Priya wants to "capitulate." What does "capitulate" most nearly mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"to give up and accept defeat","is_correct":true},{"text":"to be checkmated by the opponent","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"to retreat a piece to a safer square","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"},{"text":"to pause the game and rethink","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$to give up and accept defeat$q$, $q$The paragraph links the word to "resigning" and to the coach's rule "never surrender," so capitulate means to give up. Being checkmated is the outcome she would avoid by capitulating, not the act itself.$q$, 'draft', 'd3f73304-a08e-58b6-95d5-044d1fa76b4a')
