   $q$In paragraph 1, radio waves "attenuate" over long distances. What does "attenuate" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"to grow weaker","is_correct":true},{"text":"to change direction","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"},{"text":"to grow louder","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"to travel faster","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$to grow weaker$q$, $q$The waves "spread out" until the arriving power is "a tiny fraction" of a light bulb's energy, so attenuate means to grow weaker. Nothing in the paragraph describes the waves turning or changing course.$q$, 'draft', 'b5daaae5-9194-5836-95e3-35c06ad73cef')
