   $q$What can be inferred from the final paragraph about the food makers' new phrase?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It means the same thing as \"use by\" and will replace that label on meat.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The makers believe wording affects whether food is thrown away, but its effect is unknown.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It was adopted because the study proved shoppers ignore all date labels.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It has been shown to reduce waste more than the institute's one-page guide.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The makers believe wording affects whether food is thrown away, but its effect is unknown.$q$, $q$The makers chose the phrase "hoping it will sound less like a warning," which shows they think wording influences behavior, yet the researchers "have not yet tested" it. Because it is untested, the claim that it outperforms the guide contradicts the text.$q$, 'draft', '62364ea3-50e5-5cde-823f-94a681738d37')
