   $q$Priya was "convinced that her vase was shattering into a million pieces behind the steel door." What does this hyperbole convey?$q$, $q$[{"text":"How intensely she worried about the vase while she waited","is_correct":true},{"text":"That the kiln had actually exploded during the firing","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"How confident she felt that the firing would go perfectly","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"That the vase was made of many small pieces glued together","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$How intensely she worried about the vase while she waited$q$, $q$"A million pieces" is an exaggeration that shows the size of her anxiety during two days of waiting. The vase comes out whole with one thin crack, so nothing literally shattered.$q$, 'draft', '26d626ff-d221-5dbe-8f99-4fd15162e07d')
