   $q$Mr. Osei says, "What you paint on is a rumor. The kiln tells the truth." What does he mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Glaze must be applied quietly so that it dries evenly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Students often spread false stories about whose work is best.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The kiln changes every glaze into the same deep blue color.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"},{"text":"A raw glaze's look is unreliable until firing reveals its real color.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A raw glaze's look is unreliable until firing reveals its real color.$q$, $q$The raw glaze "looked ... like gray mud" but became "a deep blue," so the unfired color is like an unconfirmed rumor and the fired result is the truth. Nothing suggests every glaze turns blue; this one simply revealed its real color.$q$, 'draft', '26d626ff-d221-5dbe-8f99-4fd15162e07d')
