   $q$The boat wobbled "as if it could not decide which bank it preferred." What does this personification describe?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The coxswain kept steering toward the wrong shore.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The boat rocked unsteadily from one side to the other.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The boat moved in a straight and steady line.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The rowers argued about where to end their practice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The boat rocked unsteadily from one side to the other.$q$, $q$The phrase follows "wobbling from side to side," so the boat leaning toward one bank and then the other shows instability. No one in the passage argues about where to row.$q$, 'draft', '82ef284f-3030-5958-9564-1bbb52a0a775')
