  ('f3429b20-ce39-5048-8f38-3d3b8dea15ac', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-figurative-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The change asked towns "to give up a little accuracy in exchange for a great deal of agreement." What does this contrast suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Time zones made clocks far more precise than solar time was.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Towns lost nothing at all by switching to the new system.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Most towns refused the trade because accuracy mattered more.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"A small loss of local precision was worth widely shared time.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A small loss of local precision was worth widely shared time.$q$, $q$The pairing of "a little" with "a great deal" frames the trade as clearly worthwhile: clocks drifted slightly from the sun, but everyone in a zone matched. Towns did give something up, since official noon "no longer matched the sun overhead."$q$, 'draft', '5b4a954b-e234-57ca-8bbc-c282b017bb02')
