  ('dc68ea74-1a91-5379-ae85-4fda7f04fe8b', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The author says the zones "seem as natural as the sunrise" but are "one of the most successful agreements people have ever made." What is the effect of this contrast?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It hints that the agreement is weak and will soon be replaced.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It argues that time zones are set by the sun and need no human decision.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It reveals that a human invention has become so familiar it feels natural.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It suggests that sunrise happens at the same moment everywhere on Earth.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It reveals that a human invention has become so familiar it feels natural.$q$, $q$The simile shows how ordinary zones feel, and the word "agreements" reminds readers that people created them, which highlights how complete their success has been. The whole passage describes zones being chosen and adopted, so they are not set by nature.$q$, 'draft', '5b4a954b-e234-57ca-8bbc-c282b017bb02')
