   $q$The pharmacy's vocabulary "was a locked room to him. Lucia held the key." What does this metaphor suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Her grandfather could not speak any language besides Spanish.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Lucia was trusted to unlock the pharmacy each Saturday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Medical terms shut him out, and Lucia could give him access.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Her grandfather refused to let Lucia hear his private business.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Medical terms shut him out, and Lucia could give him access.$q$, $q$The locked room stands for specialized terms like "dosages and interactions" that he cannot enter, and Lucia's translating is the key. He argues "in three languages," so he is not limited to Spanish.$q$, 'draft', '86b331d4-0106-5eee-abe8-a5909b2a91ff')
