-- Passage rg12-literary-structure-pov-p02
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('3ec31ea2-aa88-543c-afa9-4ea25ff7b8e2', 'rg12-literary-structure-pov-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Survey of the Retreating Ice$q$, $q$This year the stake we drove in June
stands thirty paces from the ice,
its orange flag a stubborn tune
the wind keeps playing, once, then twice.

My mentor drove her stake in stone
the summer that my mother wed;
she measured, logged, and walked alone
to where the blue edge used to spread.

Her notebook, water-stained and thin,
records the distance, year by year,
in numbers penciled small and in
a hand that never once shows fear.

She never wrote that it was sad.
She wrote the date, the pace, the line.
She trusted numbers, all she had,
to speak more plainly than a sign.

I copy out her method now:
the compass bearing, then the tape,
the photograph from the same brow
of granite, framing the same shape.

And when I pace the gap today,
I write the date, the pace, the line,
and do not write the word I'd say
if any of these words were mine.

This year the stake we drove in June
stands thirty paces from the ice.
Next year we'll drive another soon,
and count, and write it down, and twice.$q$, 'draft')
