   $q$The club says "a small amount of river entered the boat." What is the main effect of this wording?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that the leak really was small and caused the crew no real problems.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It uses understatement to make a sinking boat sound minor, which creates humor.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It blames the river for the accident so the club can avoid paying for repairs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It uses technical rowing language so expert readers will trust the report.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It uses understatement to make a sinking boat sound minor, which creates humor.$q$, $q$The water rises to the crew's ankles and the boat has to be rescued, so "a small amount" deliberately shrinks a disaster. The report never mentions who pays for repairs.$q$, 'draft', 'fa642568-bf70-5126-804d-ecbee9e0b069')
