values
  ('c99f7fcb-4df2-56a3-8a2f-27f22027c6e8', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The sparrow's only reply to the tower is that "the gap was warm." How does this brief response affect the reader's view of the two characters?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The sparrow's simple, unbothered answer makes the tower's long boast look self-important.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The sparrow's short answer shows it plans to take revenge on the tower later.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The sparrow's short answer shows it agrees that it is small and unimportant.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The sparrow's short answer shows it is too frightened of the tower to argue back.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The sparrow's simple, unbothered answer makes the tower's long boast look self-important.$q$, $q$The sparrow is "busy with twigs" and ignores the insult, which contrasts with the tower's grand speech. Nothing suggests fear, agreement, or a plan for revenge.$q$, 'draft', '82995920-1dae-53b5-b0f3-13fc0535d6a7')
