  ('6ec8ccd8-9be3-5332-bbea-5aa80bfb9905', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The narrator says the comet's fixed position shows "remarkable patience." How does this explanation reveal the narrator's point of view?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He carefully tests his theory against the evidence and admits it might be wrong.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"takes-speaker-literally"},{"text":"He jokes about the comet because he already knows it is only a smudge.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-irony"},{"text":"He bends an obvious warning sign into praise because he badly wants the discovery to be real.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He uses a scientific term that astronomers apply to comets that move slowly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He bends an obvious warning sign into praise because he badly wants the discovery to be real.$q$, $q$A comet that stays fixed against a porch railing is a clue to a lens problem, but he turns it into a compliment. His later entries show he is sincere, not joking.$q$, 'draft', '292d4398-3385-5e97-9236-fc0ae5fd6afc')
