  ('08579fc8-c486-5075-9b36-06672e5e69bb', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The line "I do not hurry. I do not slow." appears in the second stanza and again in the last. What is the effect of its return?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It proves the metronome is broken, since it repeats itself without meaning to.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It shows that nothing has changed in the room, so the girl will quit just as her father did.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It sets up the speaker's steady self-image so that the final slip into feeling stands out.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It marks a flashback to the father's lessons, so the last stanza takes place years earlier.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It sets up the speaker's steady self-image so that the final slip into feeling stands out.$q$, $q$The repeated claim of steadiness comes just before "oh, / I must have lost count," so the break in control is sharpened by the contrast. The last stanza happens "tonight," not in the past.$q$, 'draft', '17f4d92d-1a54-5d2c-9ec9-97ba34d2b3c2')
