   $q$How does the fourth paragraph contribute to the development of the central idea?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It reverses the central idea by showing that the project failed and the village returned to truck deliveries.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-contrast"},{"text":"It introduces a new central idea about the dangers of dust and salt for coastal communities.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"It qualifies the success story by naming the conditions and upkeep the nets require, so the claim stays balanced.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It explains the scientific process by which droplets merge on the mesh and run into the gutter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It qualifies the success story by naming the conditions and upkeep the nets require, so the claim stays balanced.$q$, $q$Paragraph 4 admits that the nets need fog, wind and cleaning, and that trucks still come in dry weeks, which limits rather than cancels the success. The village did not return to trucks entirely, as paragraph 5 shows.$q$, 'draft', '725e12f5-6347-5846-a7d8-5b61e97b87ea')
