   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Early wheelchair basketball used heavy hospital chairs until manufacturers designed new ones on their own and then taught players how to use them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Early wheelchair basketball used heavy hospital chairs. Athletes worked with builders to create lighter chairs with lower seats and angled wheels, which made play faster and changed the sport's strategies.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Angling the tops of a chair's wheels inward, called camber, widens its base at the floor. This makes the chair harder to tip and allows tighter turns.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Early wheelchair basketball used heavy hospital chairs, which was unfair to athletes. Thanks to heroic players like Okafor, the sport finally became worth watching for fans everywhere.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Early wheelchair basketball used heavy hospital chairs. Athletes worked with builders to create lighter chairs with lower seats and angled wheels, which made play faster and changed the sport's strategies.$q$, $q$The first choice covers the starting point, the cooperative changes and their effect on the game. The fourth reverses the passage, which says change "came largely from the athletes themselves."$q$, 'draft', '466576c1-bad1-576d-8384-9b3c0b9d2894')
