   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Many old wax cylinders are fragile, so the archive copies them by playing each one very slowly with a softer needle before the wax decays.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"A camera measures the depth of a cylinder's groove at thousands of points. Software calculates how a needle would move and converts that motion into sound.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Many old wax cylinders are fragile, and it is a tragedy that so many were neglected. Every museum has a duty to fund light scanning before these priceless voices are lost forever.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Many old wax cylinders are too fragile to play safely with needles. An archive now scans them with light and uses software to rebuild their sound, a slow method that preserves recordings without harm.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Many old wax cylinders are too fragile to play safely with needles. An archive now scans them with light and uses software to rebuild their sound, a slow method that preserves recordings without harm.$q$, $q$The first choice states the problem, the solution and its trade-off without opinion. The fourth misstates the method, which uses light and never touches the cylinder.$q$, 'draft', 'b7112449-849e-5ec4-9e62-f4682a0e6017')
