   $q$What does the speaker conclude from the way the grandmother recorded days with no rain?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She was worried about drought and tracked dry days with special care.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She treated even an absence of rain as a measurement to record exactly.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She thought dry days were not worth including in the ledger.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"She was too busy on dry days to measure the rain gauge properly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She treated even an absence of rain as a measurement to record exactly.$q$, $q$She wrote "0.00," never a blank, "as if nothing were also something worth measuring." The poem never mentions drought, so worry is an unsupported reason for her precision.$q$, 'draft', '863dcbbe-f409-542b-80cc-cc7ac437f75f')
