   $q$Which inference about Nadia's decision to accept the draw is best supported by the text?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She accepted mainly because Coach Kim had told her to take all draws.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She believed her position was actually lost and wanted to escape it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"She accepted because a draw guaranteed that Ridgeview would win.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"She chose a certain result over a risky win, given her clock and Marcus's game.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She chose a certain result over a risky win, given her clock and Marcus's game.$q$, $q$She weighs her shrinking time and glances at board three before shaking hands, which shows she chose the safe half point over a risky attempt to win. The passage states that a draw guaranteed only a tie or better, not a win.$q$, 'draft', '37cd2a2f-789d-5ae3-882f-1bcb1ddcd067')
