   $q$Which statement best describes what the final paragraph leaves uncertain?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Whether Marcus lost his game on board three after Nadia's draw","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"Whether Nadia finds a winning line and how she feels about her choice","is_correct":true},{"text":"Whether the match between Ridgeview and Westbrook ended in a tie","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"Whether Nadia was really a pawn ahead when she accepted the draw","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Whether Nadia finds a winning line and how she feels about her choice$q$, $q$The narrator says she "did not say whether she had found the win," and her replaying of the position hints at doubt without confirming regret. Marcus's loss and the tied match are both stated directly, so they are not uncertain.$q$, 'draft', '37cd2a2f-789d-5ae3-882f-1bcb1ddcd067')
