   $q$Why does the speaker change the cloud estimate from forty to fifty?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Fifty is a rounder number and easier for the scientists to work with.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The form required the answer to be written in multiples of ten.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The moving cloud edge made fifty seem a more accurate estimate.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The speaker wanted to explain why the count was lower than the cousin's.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The moving cloud edge made fifty seem a more accurate estimate.$q$, $q$The poem gives the reason: "the edge of the cloud kept moving / and fifty felt closer to the truth." Using clouds to excuse a lower count is never suggested; the speaker defends the count simply as "what I saw."$q$, 'draft', '00982fa1-3251-5590-803f-299382e8b1d7')
