   $q$Which conclusion about who arranged the early bell is best supported, and how certain can a reader be?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Theo called from the boat, which is why he asked about rowing back.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The groundskeeper acted entirely on his own, since he had seen the fog.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-evidence"},{"text":"Coach Delgado probably phoned the groundskeeper, but the passage never confirms it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Imani radioed the groundskeeper herself, as the final sentence confirms.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Coach Delgado probably phoned the groundskeeper, but the passage never confirms it.$q$, $q$The stranded coach had reason to call for help, and the groundskeeper holds a phone, yet he "did not say who had called him," so the inference is likely but unconfirmed. The passage gives no sign that Imani or Theo made any call.$q$, 'draft', '730fe2b5-2ffd-5f0f-bd80-34f061e7e099')
