-- Passage rg12-story-details-inference-p07
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('af5efd6f-5f04-5752-b0f7-8613cd7984a3', 'rg12-story-details-inference-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-story-details-inference'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Hand Times$q$, $q$The finish camera at the district meet had worked perfectly all afternoon, which was why nobody noticed when it stopped. The head official, Mrs. Abernathy, discovered the problem only when she looked at her screen after the girls' 800 meters and found a frozen image of an empty track.

Kenji Watanabe had been assigned to the backup station, a folding chair beside the finish line with three stopwatches on a clipboard. He had been told it was a formality. For two hours he had clicked the watches dutifully, writing numbers that he assumed no one would ever read.

Now Mrs. Abernathy was walking toward him.

The race had ended close. Ruth Asante, who ran for Kenji's school, and a girl from Carver named Sofia Lindgren had leaned at the line together, shoulder to shoulder. Kenji had been timing both. His watches read 2:14.6 for Ruth and 2:14.7 for Sofia.

"What do you have?" Mrs. Abernathy asked.

Kenji looked at the numbers. A tenth of a second was the gap. He also remembered the training sheet he had skimmed that morning, which said that a person starting and stopping a watch by hand could be off by two or three tenths without noticing. He remembered, too, that Ruth had been his lab partner in chemistry all last year, and that she had helped him pass.

"Ruth is a tenth ahead on my watches," he said. "But I can't honestly say I'm sure about a tenth. I'd call it even."

Mrs. Abernathy studied him for a moment, then nodded and wrote something on her own clipboard. Twenty minutes later, the board announced a tie for first, and both girls received gold ribbons.

On the bus home, Ruth sat several rows ahead of him. When they reached the school parking lot, she stopped beside his seat, looked as if she might say something, and then simply knocked twice on the seat back and walked off the bus.$q$, 'draft')
