   $q$What does the detail of the father laughing "at the right moment" add to the poem's development?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows the father has his own ways of understanding, which begins to complicate the idea that he depends entirely on the speaker.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that the father is pretending to understand so that the clerk will not notice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-character"},{"text":"It proves that the speaker translated the jokes perfectly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It suggests that the clerk is making fun of the father and the speaker.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows the father has his own ways of understanding, which begins to complicate the idea that he depends entirely on the speaker.$q$, $q$The father reads faces "by listening past the noise," a skill the speaker lacks, which prepares the ending's question of who is helping whom. The speaker says "I translate the words and lose the jokes," so the jokes were not translated.$q$, 'draft', '03aa796a-0ab7-593c-a290-c6cc033d038e')
