   $q$How does the first paragraph set up the idea the passage later challenges?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that Ji-ho has no experience with design or testing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It suggests that the volunteer group does not care about the children it serves.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It presents Ji-ho's confidence in measured grip strength as the true sign of quality.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It reveals that Amara's family asked specifically for a gray hand.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It presents Ji-ho's confidence in measured grip strength as the true sign of quality.$q$, $q$Ji-ho tests until "the numbers held steady" and arrives "certain of its quality," a belief the story then questions. He clearly has design experience, so the second choice contradicts the text.$q$, 'draft', '94c40bda-aadc-5df1-9bef-f79653aa3c85')
