   $q$Which statement best expresses a central theme of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Cranes migrate north every spring after resting along a river.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-theme"},{"text":"Young people should stay close to home rather than move far away for school.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Grandparents become lonely and sad when their grandchildren grow up.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Belonging to a place and its people can be carried with us, even when we leave.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Belonging to a place and its people can be carried with us, even when we leave.$q$, $q$The speaker learns that "a place can belong to you / without keeping you," so leaving does not end belonging. The migration choice states the subject, not a message.$q$, 'draft', 'b5945d61-2ba0-5c29-8d89-fade7d73d655')
