   $q$Which statement best expresses a central theme of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Laundromats are noisy, crowded places that few people enjoy visiting.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Photographs of objects are always sadder than photographs of people.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"},{"text":"Old businesses should never be allowed to close in a neighborhood.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"A community lives in its relationships, which can continue even when the place that held them is lost.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A community lives in its relationships, which can continue even when the place that held them is lost.$q$, $q$The people keep their friendships and routines going elsewhere, and the caption says "Everything else moved." The passage does not argue that businesses must never close.$q$, 'draft', '7aaa60c9-4dd2-53dd-94f3-8c7341e558e5')
