   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the fable?$q$, $q$[{"text":"After a rockslide, the young marmots ignore Teska and build their own colony elsewhere.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"A selfish old marmot finally gets what she deserves when a rockslide humbles her.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Teska tells young marmots to dig where the snow leaves last.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Teska guards her knowledge with riddles until a rockslide forces her to rely on the young, and sharing what she knows leads to a joint map.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Teska guards her knowledge with riddles until a rockslide forces her to rely on the young, and sharing what she knows leads to a joint map.$q$, $q$The correct choice covers her hoarding, the turning point, and the shared map without judgment. "Selfish" and "gets what she deserves" are opinions, and the young marmots do not leave.$q$, 'draft', '14de3638-bd5a-502a-a9c5-697b5d2d8f23')
