   $q$How does the final paragraph deepen the fable's message beyond the shared map?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that the young marmots now ask Teska more questions than ever before.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It contrasts being needed with being valued: fewer questions but more visits show company replacing dependence.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It suggests that Teska regrets sharing her knowledge and wants her old role back.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"It shows that Teska is lonely because no one needs her advice any longer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-ending"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It contrasts being needed with being valued: fewer questions but more visits show company replacing dependence.$q$, $q$"Asked fewer questions" yet "visited more" shows that sharing traded dependence for genuine companionship. The visits and her surprise rule out loneliness and regret.$q$, 'draft', '14de3638-bd5a-502a-a9c5-697b5d2d8f23')
